Abstarction

-hiding the internal implementation and exposing the relevant details.

java allows two ways to abstract

-abstract classess :  allows us to create both abstract methods and Implemented method.

-interface

Abstract classes:
syntax:
abstract class className{
//methods --can be create  in two types

1.method with Implementation or concrete method
example:
public void do(){
//Implementation logic
}

2.method without Implementation or abstract method
example:
public void dotask();

//variables
//constructors

}


object creation is not possible for the abstract class
but we can create object for the class which extends the abstract class.

abstract class always begin with the abstract keyword.
and also required the abstract keyword while creating the methods in the abstract which are abstract methods.

abstract class which extended by the concrete class must and should provide the implementation for the unimplemented method in the extended class.



 